      "id": 100,
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## Cilium Datapath \u2014 live in-kernel\n\nCilium replaces kube-proxy and the Linux bridge with an eBPF datapath that runs **inside the kernel network stack**. Every flow, every policy decision, every load-balanced connection is decided by BPF programs attached to network hooks.\n\nThis dashboard shows that datapath at work. Most of what's here would require kprobe instrumentation or pcap captures on a non-eBPF network stack."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Flow volume + drops \u2014 what the kernel datapath is doing",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "id": 110,
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Flows/sec",
      "description": "Every L3/L4 flow Cilium observed. Includes inter-pod, ingress, egress.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "id": 111,
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(hubble_flows_processed_total[2m])) or vector(0)"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
