    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 44
      },
      "id": 131,
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**TCP flag distribution** is one of those signals that's effectively impossible to surface without eBPF in the datapath. Every connection state transition (SYN, SYN-ACK, FIN, RST) tells you about TCP health: lots of RST = something is aborting connections rudely; SYN without ACK = connection refused."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "TCP flags/sec \u2014 every state transition",
      "description": "SYN = new connection attempts. RST = aborted connections. FIN = clean shutdowns. The mix tells you protocol health at a glance.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 48
      },
      "id": 132,
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (flag) (rate(hubble_tcp_flags_total[2m])) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "{{flag}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "cps",
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 25,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal"
            }
          }
        }
      }
